{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504855-any-one-know-how-not-to-play-lovecraftian-cultists-and-sorcerers","id":1504855,"title":"Any one know how not to play Lovecraftian cultists and sorcerers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-08T10:28:57-08:00","id":1504855,"title":"Any one know how not to play Lovecraftian cultists and sorcerers?","content":"Kind of as the title says. I can't help but feel that the characters in this game are basically the same as the cultists and sorcerers in my Call of Cthulhu games. The world is not what we think it is nor does it work the way we think. There is magic, but it drives observers either don't remember it or go mad from understanding it. And the Mages are actively working to bring the truth to the masses. Heck, an argument could be made that the Seers are the actual good guys and all we are getting is the Pentacle's propaganda saying they are 'oppressors.'<br /> <br /> Anyone change the rules to make the setting not so anathma to the sleepers and what did you do to accomplish it with the rules?<br /> <br /> (I'm already contemplating just eliminating the dissonance for sleepers and just keeping the forgetfulness)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T11:00:04-08:00","id":1504857,"title":"","content":"I think I proposed something similar but for different reason. My biggest dissonance with both the older and newer Worlds of Darkness was how they liked to portray &quot;mainstream humanity&quot; as skeptical and rational when even back in the 90s there were UFO crazes, there was Y2K hysteria, Christian Nationalists were convincing thousands that some &quot;new world order&quot; was bringing Armageddon upon the world, etc. I tried to argue that people (or sleepers) were, if anything, not skeptical enough and too willing to believe anything.<br /> <br /> The response was that I was changing a fundamental aspect of the game and throwing everything out of whack. That was a while ago, so maybe opinions have changed, maybe.<br /> <br /> As for the Seers being &quot;good guys,&quot; get the book <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/60246/Seers-of-the-Throne?term=seers+of+the+\" target=\"_blank\">Seers of the Throne</a>. The book literally says &quot;Despots are expected to behave like despots,&quot; and will clear up any arguments about &quot;Pentacle propaganda.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 03-09-2023, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T13:07:37-08:00","id":1504866,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I don't quite understand where your intuition comes from.<br /> <br /> The vibe of the Cthulhu mythos more closely matches the Abyss which threatens to undo reality and replace it with raw chaos. Supernal magic is not intrinsically maddening though it is awe-inspiring. Magic represents suppressed human potential. The effect that exposure to magic has on Sleepers is the very definition of the Lie. Reality is constructed by gods of tyranny and totalitarianism. The Seers are those mages who have sold out and agreed to be enforcers of the prison reality - with all its oppression and suffering - in exchange for worldly pleasures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T13:40:27-08:00","id":1504868,"title":"","content":"Yes, the mages here are closer to Eibon, etc., than your typical wizard (though I\u2019d say they\u2019re even closer to Doctor Frankenstein\u2019s ilk). Yog-Sothoth might as well be Pandemonium itself.<br /> <br /> I fully embrace this idea, but to make a setting that goes against it\u2026 yeah, tweak the Sleeper rules first. Though I\u2019d remove the memory/madness thing first and not the spell-degradation part.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, Seers being the good guys? Uhh\u2026 not only I do not understand how that makes the setting less Cosmic Horror-ish, it would require significantly more re-imagining the background setting (than simply making it less Cosmic Horror) to make the priesthood of tyranny into the good guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T13:45:25-08:00","id":1504869,"title":"","content":"I second the notion, Supernal magic is not inherently bad, the Lie and the Curse make it hurt, they make people break and desperately try to delude themselves that they saw something else.<br /> <br /> But regarding playing them, I think the easiest ones to use are the Secret Order of the Gate, which are found in the <i>Seers of the Throne</i> book. I would also default to the Rapt (who have spiritually broken and in their madness become a conduit for unconstrained magic to burn its way into the world) and the Scelesti (those who engage in the pyrrhic endeavor of channeling the power of things that cannot be) and the Tremere (soul eaters who dance with perdition for immortality, while risking being devoured by an ineffable hunger). All three of them are covered in great detail in <i>Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T13:51:34-08:00","id":1504872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leofwyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504855-any-one-know-how-not-to-play-lovecraftian-cultists-and-sorcerers#post1504855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of as the title says. I can't help but feel that the characters in this game are basically the same as the cultists and sorcerers in my Call of Cthulhu games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to a degree that's kinda the point. Like, each of the CofD lines is about playing a version of a monster from pop culture. Awakening is about playing wizards, so the Lovecraftian cultist is certainly a common strand of inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Mages are actively working to bring the truth to the masses. </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Like, that's the plan for some of the Orders, but they're all aware that it's not that easy. Sleepers going mad is <i>not </i>the plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heck, an argument could be made that the Seers are the actual good guys and all we are getting is the Pentacle's propaganda saying they are 'oppressors.' </div> </div> </div>As has already been said, no (I get the impulse, but as written, the Seers are not subtle). The Seers serve precisely the entities that cause sleepers to go mad when they see magic. Remember, there's a halfway state for humans between sleeper and mage, the sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone change the rules to make the setting not so anathma to the sleepers and what did you do to accomplish it with the rules?<br /> <br /> (I'm already contemplating just eliminating the dissonance for sleepers and just keeping the forgetfulness) </div> </div> </div>I've wondered about that, but the difficulty is that you're actually handing even more power over to Mages. In practice magic interacting violently with sleepers is a limitation for mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T14:15:20-08:00","id":1504879,"title":"","content":"Guardians of the Veil are the ones with the agenda of trying to keep Sleepers from knowing about magic for their own good. That niche is on the Pentacle side.<br /> <br /> Seers of the Throne might occasionally sell that line to people they're trying to recruit, but internally they're not concerned with Sleeper safety beyond continuing to exist so that they can be exploited.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle includes the group that tries to keep people from learning knowledge that will damage them, the Seers apply an attitude of &quot;what you don't know won't kill you&quot; to secretly using cheap toxic plastics in children's toys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T18:18:51-08:00","id":1504888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leofwyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504855-any-one-know-how-not-to-play-lovecraftian-cultists-and-sorcerers#post1504855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of as the title says. I can't help but feel that the characters in this game are basically the same as the cultists and sorcerers in my Call of Cthulhu games. The world is not what we think it is nor does it work the way we think. There is magic, but it drives observers either don't remember it or go mad from understanding it. And the Mages are actively working to bring the truth to the masses. Heck, an argument could be made that the Seers are the actual good guys and all we are getting is the Pentacle's propaganda saying they are 'oppressors.'<br /> <br /> Anyone change the rules to make the setting not so anathma to the sleepers and what did you do to accomplish it with the rules?<br /> <br /> (I'm already contemplating just eliminating the dissonance for sleepers and just keeping the forgetfulness)</div> </div> </div> </div>Before considering that, you might want to take a second to consider the fact that Dissonance is just the extreme end of the general nature of magic and the supernatural in Chronicles running into the gamification of the general nature of occultic practices in the real world leaning towards the sacred and profane (as various practices and backgrounds understand and approach it) that shouldn't or can't be shared with the populace-ie, pretty much all of it is inherently hostile and not psychologically healthy for people to experience. It's not so much a cosmic horror thing with that, mind, though it definitely has some of those shades- more that it enforces the games general themes of humanity versus monstrosity and makes it clear that being a monster is intended to be a cause of stress and and strife for anyone who values it. It's also the background explanation for what keeps the world in a state of urban horror with a masquerade-people know the world has monsters and magic, but so long as direct confrontation with it is always going to fuck with your head, integration's not really on the table.<br /> <br /> Mages, being defined as people who are and do magic, are the most extreme end of that subject, and thusly reinforces their metaphorical and metaphysical role as the 1%, and firmly cements both the isolation and the careless excess of that role-their very nature makes being part of the sleeper communities they used to be part of, their ability to work miracles in a mysterious capacity makes them vaunted and elevated to those same sleepers, and a big part of their monstrosity comes from the way they become increasingly willing to wreck the heads of sleepers in pursuit of their interests and needs.<br /> <br /> This is one of those things where I would actually argue that if that's a deal breaker for you, you might just flat out need a different urban fantasy/horror setting. The conceit it's founded on is one of those things go right down to the roots of the game's design.<br /> <br /> As for the Seers being right, you can burn that angle of understanding to ashes. What you're probably looking for is the argument that the Guardians and the more sleeper-concious part of the Mysterium are right. The Seers are <i>in favor</i> of Dissonance being the default-all the better to keep people away from Awakening-and their policies aren't motivated by concern for sleeper safety so much as ensuring those who have power don't have to contend against others suddenly getting to bite at the pie. The Tyrant imposing a police state isn't doing it for anyone's safety but their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T20:10:16-08:00","id":1504896,"title":"","content":"Besides what has already been explained in previous posts, do remember that Legacy Attainments bypass the usual dangers of Paradox/Dissonance/Quiescence. They can still provoke Breaking Points for Integrity, except without the mandatory amnesia/rationalization at the end of the scene. Also, nothing forbids a Mage from relying on &quot;lower magic&quot; in the sense of the rituals available to all mortals as described in ChroD Core, like Summoning, Abjuration and Warding+Binding. Mages just cannot have Supernatural Merits like Telekinesis and Telepathy, but Sleepwalkers can, which is one of the reasons that Mages employ such individuals.For more examples of mortal-tier, non-Supernal and non-Abyssal magic that Mages can rely on, consider consulting Second Sight supplement for ChroD 1ed (back when it was still called NWOD), Summoners supplement for Mage 1ed, and the Hurt Locker supplement for ChroD 2ed.<br /> <br /> You can also find 2ed updates for Second Sight and Summoners in the Storyteller's Vault, under the names of Third Eye and Deals With Darkness, respectively. Last but not least, Geist 2ed also has necromancy rituals that are also mortal-tier, in the form of Ceremonies. Do keep in mind that all of this &quot;lower magic&quot; still has the risk of causing Breaking Points, but that is mainly for Sleepers who do not dabble in the occult. Sleepwalkers and Proximi are exposed to all kinds of magic so regularly that only the most maddening and horrifying types stand a chance to make them suffer Breaking Points. I'd link threads on these forums that have homebrewed Supernatural Merits, but the thrice-accursed spam-detection bots are not working properly, so just search for &quot;Amechra's Homebrew Hub&quot; and &quot;Advanced Supernatural Merits ... and Styled Supernatural Merits!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T11:44:49-08:00","id":1504960,"title":"","content":"I am a long term OWoD player. I remember when the Technocracy were &quot;the bad guys&quot; as described by the books...until they were described as maybe grey...and the traditions were/are just as bad or worse...to now it was all (possibly) the Nephandi. Just as the original Mage the Ascension books were told from a certain point of view - I read this core book for Awakening the same way. (2nd edition Core is all I have) Forgive me if, at this point, I can't seem to read any of the books of either game line (WoD or CoD) without believing that I am being mislead. <br /> <br /> As for playing a different game - I was trying to get a more Dresden Files/Sandman/Hellblazer vibe. I've played Ars Magica and Mage the Ascension. I have CJ Carella's Witchcraft that is out of print and doesn't do what I want. I don't like FATE so I am not going to use the Dresden Files rpg in any of it's forms. This game cures many of my issues with Mage the Ascension...I like rotes here, I like the Arcana here more, I like mana as a resource controlling Arcana beyond the 2 (Three with Legacy) that are your Mage's strong suits. I like that arcana are part of the roll. I like the dice mechanics a HECK of a lot more. <br /> <br /> I like 2nd edition rules...but I am trying to change the setting where the use of magic doesn't exclude having meaningful interactions with the &quot;sleepers.&quot; Spell degradation for their presence is fine and actually fits what I want to do. Was hoping to get further suggestions in that vein. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T12:02:14-08:00","id":1504963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leofwyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504855-any-one-know-how-not-to-play-lovecraftian-cultists-and-sorcerers?p=1504960#post1504960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a long term OWoD player. I remember when the Technocracy were &quot;the bad guys&quot; as described by the books...until they were described as maybe grey...and the traditions were/are just as bad or worse...to now it was all (possibly) the Nephandi. Just as the original Mage the Ascension books were told from a certain point of view - I read this core book for Awakening the same way. (2nd edition Core is all I have) Forgive me if, at this point, I can't seem to read any of the books of either game line (WoD or CoD) without believing that I am being mislead.<br /> <br /> As for playing a different game - I was trying to get a more Dresden Files/Sandman/Hellblazer vibe. I've played Ars Magica and Mage the Ascension. I have CJ Carella's Witchcraft that is out of print and doesn't do what I want. I don't like FATE so I am not going to use the Dresden Files rpg in any of it's forms. This game cures many of my issues with Mage the Ascension...I like rotes here, I like the Arcana here more, I like mana as a resource controlling Arcana beyond the 2 (Three with Legacy) that are your Mage's strong suits. I like that arcana are part of the roll. I like the dice mechanics a HECK of a lot more.<br /> <br /> I like 2nd edition rules...but I am trying to change the setting where the use of magic doesn't exclude having meaningful interactions with the &quot;sleepers.&quot; Spell degradation for their presence is fine and actually fits what I want to do. Was hoping to get further suggestions in that vein.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening learned from the mistakes of Ascension, and is therefore a lot less relative about it's moral positioning. The Pentacle may be assholes, because all mages are assholes, but the Seers, while complex and dynamic in a lot of ways, are unmistakably <i>the bad guys</i>. Chronicles is largely Grey-and-Black Morality, but is pretty crystal clear about who is what on the whole.<br /> <br /> You can have meaningful interactions with Sleepers, you're just not going to get away with throwing a fireball around a non-Sleepwalker. You can even go on investigations or infiltrations with Sleepers, and even get away with a siege-you just have to be responsible with your magic.<br /> <br /> As for adjustments, I'm probably not going to be too helpful, but as way to start getting the vibe, do you want to keep the way Awakening mages has them as monsters and Awakening as a horror game at about the same level as it is now, are you hoping to actually ramp it up but in a different way, or are you looking to just drop it down lower or all together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T07:25:52-07:00","id":1505249,"title":"","content":"Want to keep the hubris and obsessions of the mages...but maybe dial down the horror. More urban fantasy like dresden files. I don't want something on the level that ascension gets to with other plant colonies (and especially not the anti-technology vibe). Mages dealing with other mages, dealing with monsters whose predations on humanity risk everyone's safety. (The vampire club in downtown having its willing blood dolls is ok...a vampire serial killer not so much)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27377-leofwyn","name":"Leofwyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T11:44:00-07:00","id":1505262,"title":"","content":"You may not want to hear this, but Mage: the Awakening may be the wrong game for you if you just want &quot;Dresden Files&quot; urban fantasy. Chronicles of Darkness might be more fitting, if you use Second Sight: Third Eye for &quot;low magic,&quot; and take the rituals and ceremonies for Krewes (Geist) and Sorcerers (Mummy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T18:25:31-07:00","id":1505271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1504855-any-one-know-how-not-to-play-lovecraftian-cultists-and-sorcerers?p=1505262#post1505262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not want to hear this, but Mage: the Awakening may be the wrong game for you if you just want &quot;Dresden Files&quot; urban fantasy. Chronicles of Darkness might be more fitting, if you use Second Sight: Third Eye for &quot;low magic,&quot; and take the rituals and ceremonies for Krewes (Geist) and Sorcerers (Mummy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Proximi can be great for that low power niche, low power utility spells and their curse make for an interesting feel of power at a cost. I would also add <i>Hurt Locker</i> to the resources. It has some excellent minor templates and cool plot hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" targ